  "description": "A .NET library for building Rust applications inside a Linux Docker container, so the machine needs a running Docker engine but no Rust tools. Checks that the engine is reachable and returns operating-system-specific guidance when it is not; prepares the build image from the official rust image with optional generated layers for extra system packages, clippy and rustfmt, a pinned Rust version, and Windows and Android cross-compilation; starts labelled build containers with persistent cargo cache volumes; copies the project source in, applies a license policy and runs cargo inside the container with typed diagnostics, progress and test results; copies executables and native libraries out (optionally in the NuGet runtimes layout); does it all in one call for several targets; and cleans up everything it created.",
